{"id":28150,"slug":"stalker","title":"Stalker","year":1979,"country":"Soviet Union","duration":161,"spine":888,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/28150-stalker","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/a2edcc26e1eab799429c48ff7067cee7/E0TPdmb6xXiqaiuPmArJq90hdAs3xV_large.jpg","description":"Andrei Tarkovsky’s final Soviet feature is a metaphys­ical journey through an enigmatic postapocalyptic landscape, and a rarefied cinematic experience like no other. A hired guide—the Stalker—leads a writer and a professor into the heart of the Zone, the restricted site of a long-ago disaster, where the three men eventually zero in on the Room, a place rumored to fulfill one’s most deeply held desires. Adapting a science-fiction novel by Arkady and Boris Strugatsky, Tarkovsky created an immersive world with a wealth of material detail and a sense of organic atmosphere. A religious allegory, a reflection of contemporaneous political anxieties, a meditation on film itself—Stalker envelops the viewer by opening up a multitude of possible meanings.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Andrei Tarkovsky","slug":"andrei-tarkovsky"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Alisa Freindlikh","role":"The Stalker’s wife","slug":"alisa-freindlikh"},{"actor":"Aleksandr Kaidanovsky","role":"The Stalker","slug":"aleksandr-kaidanovsky"},{"actor":"Anatoly Solonitsyn","role":"The Writer","slug":"anatoly-solonitsyn"},{"actor":"Nikolai Grinko","role":"The Professor","slug":"nikolai-grinko"},{"actor":"Natasha Abramova","role":"Monkey","slug":"natasha-abramova"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Andrei Tarkovsky","slug":"andrei-tarkovsky"},{"role":"Scenario","person":"Arkady Strugatsky","slug":null},{"role":"Scenario","person":"Boris Strugatsky","slug":null},{"role":"Cinematography","person":"Alexander Knyazhinsky","slug":null},{"role":"Art direction","person":"Andrei Tarkovsky","slug":"andrei-tarkovsky"},{"role":"Music","person":"Eduard Artemyev","slug":null},{"role":"Poems by","per